  "question": "A production database is down at 2am and the on-call DBA is not answering pages. What is the escalation path, and who has to approve emergency production database access?",
  "role": "employee",
  "answer": "If the DBA on call is unreachable after two pages, the incident commander escalates through the **Platform Engineering Manager**, who may authorise the emergency database access procedure. [C1] The DBA rotation does **not** auto-escalate. [C1] When an incident cannot be resolved without direct production database access, the break-glass procedure applies: 1. [C3]",
